config BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_CHAOSNET
	bool "cadr-chaosnet"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_COMMON
	help
	  The Chaosnet: the program on the processing system that carries
	  packets between the CADR's Chaosnet interface in the fabric and
	  the outside world.  It is the cable the interface is plugged
	  into, and nothing above that.

	  It answers no services, because a CADR holds none.  The file and
	  time host a band calls is another machine on the network, which
	  this program reaches like any other station.

	  Chaosnet over UDP puts the cable on the board's Ethernet, so
	  that host or a bridge can be a station on it.

	  It has an init script, as cadr-disk-packs and cadr-terminal do:
	  a machine that is up wants its cable up too, and nothing is on
	  the bus while no packet is moving.
